; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; B5's bombs, Step 12c.
;
; `bombArray` is $DD30, the three $10-byte slots directly after the projectile
; array, and here it is directly after `!Projs` for the same reason: the two are
; one page on the Game Boy and `clearProjectileArray` clears both. They share no
; state otherwise -- not the slot walk, not the pass, not the collision.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!Bombs        = $0630           ; $DD30. 3 x $10
!BOMB_SIZE    = $10

; Step 13a: the frame `toggleMissiles` costs. `loadGraphics` (00:$2753) ends in
; `beginGraphicsTransfer` (00:$27BA), which sets the transfer flag and calls
; `waitOneFrame` until the vblank handler has copied the $20 bytes -- one frame,
; since the queue drains 64 bytes a vblank. **The rest of the play handler runs
; on the other side of that wait**, so the original's pass is split across two
; frames and the frame between them draws nothing new.
;
; The port cannot block inside a routine without losing the commit point the
; gate counts frames by, so the split is a flag, the way `!ItemStage` is: set by
; the toggle, uploaded by NMI, and cleared by `MainLoop` on the next frame, which
; resumes the pass after `SamusTryShooting` instead of starting a new one.
!CannonHold   = $0660           ; nonzero from the toggle to the resumed frame
!CANNON_HOLD_CUTSCENE = $02     ; ...and this nonzero when the cutscene arm toggled

; 1.0 Step 8a: `loadGraphics` (00:$2753) and the vblank handler that drains it
; (`VBlank_vramDataTransfer`, 00:$2BA3). The original hands the routine a
; gfxInfo record in HL; the port hands `LoadGraphicsLong` a row of `GfxInfo`,
; which the builder fills from those records (`src/gfx_info.zig`). A row is
; resolved on the logic side into a ring entry, and NMI moves one Game Boy chunk
; of the head entry a frame: the size mod $40, or $40, which in SNES bytes is
; the remainder mod $80, or $80. The Game Boy queues one record and waits on it
; (`beginGraphicsTransfer`, 00:$27BA); a caller here queues its records and
; waits on the ring, and since the handler moves one chunk a vblank either way,
; the frames are the same. Head is NMI's to write and tail the logic's, so
; neither half needs the other masked.
!GFX_Q_LEN    = 16              ; entries: Varia's pickup queues six, the debug menu's sync seven
!GFX_Q_BYTES  = 8               ; src (3), a pad, dest word (2), bytes left (2)
; Low RAM between the OAM shadow and the Queen's, absolute from either bank.
!GfxQ         = $1220           ; `!GFX_Q_LEN` * `!GFX_Q_BYTES`
!GfxQHead     = $12A0           ; the entry NMI is moving
!GfxQTail     = $12A1           ; where the next is queued
!GfxMoved     = $12A2           ; nonzero when this vblank moved a chunk
; 1.0 Step 9: `animateGettingVaria` (00:$27E3) and the vblank half that draws it
; (`VBlank_variaAnimation`, 00:$2BF4). The destination is kept as the Game Boy's
; address, because the walk is the original's arithmetic on it; NMI maps each
; byte onto the SNES tile it lands in.
!VariaAnim    = $12A3           ; $D08C `variaAnimationFlag`: NMI animates
!VariaDest    = $12A4           ; 2, `hVramTransfer.destAddr`, a Game Boy address
!VariaHL      = $12A6           ; 2, NMI's own: the walk's HL
!VariaTmp     = $12A8           ; 2, NMI's own
!VariaSrc     = $12AA           ; 2, the suit's sheet, in
!VariaBank    = $12AC           ;    this bank
!VariaVram    = $12AD           ; 2, the SNES word its first tile lands on
; 1.0 Step 9: the last frame was a pass of `handleItemPickup_end`'s loops, which
; end in `waitForNextFrame` and so tick the clock (see `.itemFrame`).
!ItemTick     = $12AF
; 1.0 Step 11: the ordinary AIs' speed tables, as far pointers
; `ResolveProjectiles` fills at boot. See `HopArcYA` in `src/residue.zig`.
!SkreekJumpA  = $12B0           ; 3, `enemy_skreekJumpSpeeds`
!DrivelYA     = $12B3           ; 3, `enemy_drivelYSpeeds`
!DrivelXA     = $12B6           ; 3, `enemy_drivelXSpeeds`
!SineConcaveA = $12B9           ; 3, `enemy_sineConcaveSpeeds`
!SineConvexA  = $12BC           ; 3, `enemy_sineConvexSpeeds`
!EnSineField  = $12BF           ; 2, the slot byte `EnSineBack`/`Ahead` moves
!EnSineIdx    = $12C1           ; the table index they read at
; 1.0 Step 12: the blob thrower's own globals -- there is only ever one -- and
; its two blobs. Its part list and hitbox are WRAM in the cartridge ($C300,
; $C360), which it rewrites as it rises; the copies are `!BlobSprite` and
; `!BlobBox`, in high WRAM because they are read through long pointers anyway.
!BlobAction   = $12C2           ; $C380 `blobThrower_actionTimer`: the tables' index
!BlobWait     = $12C3           ; $C381 `blobThrower_waitTimer`
!BlobState    = $12C4           ; $C382 `blobThrower_state`, 0-3
!BlobFacing   = $12C5           ; $C386 `blobThrower_facingDirection`: 1, Samus left of it
!BlobThrowA   = $12C6           ; 3, `blobThrower_data`: parts, hitbox, speed tables
!BlobMovesA   = $12C9           ; 3, `blobMovementTable_A`-`D`
!BlobN        = $12CC           ; `.moveSprites`' count, the original's B
!BlobTabAt    = $12CD           ; 2, and its table, as an offset into `!BlobThrowA`
; 1.0 Step 13: Arachnus's globals ($C390-$C396). There is one Arachnus. The
; ROM's init clears seven bytes; `arachnus_unknownVar` ($C392, set to 5) and
; the two after its health are never read, so the port has no bytes for them.
!ArachJumpN   = $12CF           ; $C390 `arachnus_jumpCounter`: the index into the jump tables
!ArachTimer   = $12D0           ; $C391 `arachnus_actionTimer`
!ArachStatus  = $12D1           ; $C393 `arachnus_jumpStatus`: $00 in an arc, $80 an arc's end, $81 the last's
!ArachHealth  = $12D2           ; $C394 `arachnus_health`: bomb hits left; the slot's own is $FF
!ArachJumpA   = $12D3           ; 3, `enAI_arachnus.jumpSpeedTable_high`, `_mid` and `_low`
; 1.0 Step 14: the Gamma's. Its stun counter is its own, beside the Alpha's.
!GammaStun    = $12D6           ; $C46A `gamma_stunCounter`
!GammaAngleA  = $12D7           ; 3, `gamma_getAngleFromTable.angleTable` (01:$729C)
!GammaSpeedA  = $12DA           ; 3, `gamma_getSpeedVector`'s twenty-four arms (01:$7359)
